From 6a77611c976884293a4f71518af0f27544b4362d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:23:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] camerabin: tap to focus, ISO and exposure compensation
 on libcamerasrc, Release 13
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Without GstPhotography there were no focus, locks or exposure controls,
so jolla-camera offered neither tap to focus nor ISO. With libcamerasrc
inside the wrapper source they now work through its control properties:

- focus: the tapped area goes to af-windows (mapped from the viewfinder
  to pixel array coordinates through PixelArrayActiveAreas, assuming the
  software ISP's centred crop); a lock rescans and stays Searching until
  af-state reports the new scan as focused, 8 s at most. With the flash
  set to on, the LED lights the scan as a focus assist.
- exposure: ISO 100 to 3200 as manual analogue gain (gain 1 = ISO 100),
  automatic ISO as auto gain, compensation as exposure-value.

The active area is read once per camera from libcamera's device
provider inside the plugin; a new gsttools symbol would not link against
the SDK target's installed library.

Disclosure: LLMGD-2 · origin O1 (author asked for tap to focus and ISO as on official ports and tested both in jolla-camera, the model wrote the code)
